  "id": "eq-model-fd-derivative-limit",
  "paper": "foundations",
  "argument": "derivatives",
  "title": "The derivative as the limit of average speeds",
  "spoken": "d x by d t equals the limit, as Delta t approaches zero, of x at t plus Delta t, minus x at t, all over Delta t.",
  "explanation": "The distance covered between t and t plus Delta t, divided by Delta t, is the average speed over that interval. The derivative is the value those averages settle on as Delta t shrinks; Delta t itself is never set to zero.",
  "review": "draft",
  "notation": "modern-pedagogical",
  "unitSystem": "si",
  "live": false,
  "assumptions": [
    "The averages settle on one value as the interval shrinks, as they do for the rolling ball's 3t².",
    "A foundation lesson's worked case in modern notation; not a transcription of the printed paper."
  ],
